From 156954c446004afd2191ee7834e954cd6142d318 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: heresy <heresy@local>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 16:16:30 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1012/1259] Writing room: OpenRouter, runner presets, empty
 fields kept; style rules eased

HERESY 1012.
- Writer: the chat server under Engine, or OpenRouter (model id with the
  list of OpenRouter's models, the user's API key kept in memory unless asked
  to be remembered, sent only to openrouter.ai).
- Engine: one-click addresses for vLLM on Forge, LM Studio and Ollama, the
  local runners YuE2 Studio knows.
- An empty field in a draft means unchanged. A style-only answer came back
  with "lyrics": "" on 30.09.2026; applying it would have wiped 228 lines.
  The draft now shows the current text there and never applies a blank. The
  instructions also ask the model to return unchanged fields in full.
- Style rules eased on Viktor's word and the measurement: up to 1,600
  characters is fine (a long style agreeing with its score sang as clearly as
  a short one); ASCII -> is fine; only the Unicode arrow is flagged, with
  "write -> instead". Help texts say so, and put score agreement first.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
